{"id": "b3443bf3c312c9d144e4", "question": "Is there a full Neptunian orbit between the first two burials of women in the Panth\u00e9on?", "step_idx": 1, "options": ["A): Yes", "B): No"], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. The Panth\u00e9on is a mausoleum in Paris, France, where notable French citizens are buried.\n2. The first two women to be buried in the Panth\u00e9on were \u00c9milie du Ch\u00e2telet (1749) and Marie Curie (1995).\n3. Neptune is the eighth planet from the Sun in our solar system.\n4. The average distance from the Sun to Neptune is about 2.8 billion miles (4.5 billion kilometers).\n5. The average distance from the Earth to the Sun is about 93 million miles (150 million kilometers).\n6. The time it takes for Neptune to complete one orbit around the Sun is approximately 165 Earth years.\n7. The time between the first two burials of women in the Panth\u00e9on is 1995 - 1749 = 246 years.\n8. To find out if there is a full Neptunian orbit between the first two burials, we need to calculate how many Neptunian orbits occurred in 246 years.\n9. We can do this by dividing the time between the burials (246 years) by the length of one Neptunian orbit (165 years).\n10. 246 / 165", "initial_cot_probs": [1.05920662463177e-06, 6.553078856086358e-05], "initial_probs": [1.969504592125304e-05, 0.00016490458801854402], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 1, "rt_lambda": 1.0, "cot_step": "The Panth\u00e9on is a mausoleum in Paris, France, where notable French citizens are buried.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "The Panth\u00e9on is a mausoleum in Paris, France, where notable French citizens are buried.", "2.", "The first two women to be buried in the Panth\u00e9on were \u00c9milie du Ch\u00e2telet (1749) and Marie Curie (1995).", "3.", "Neptune is the eighth planet from the Sun in our solar system.", "4.", "The average distance from the Sun to Neptune is about 2.8 billion miles (4.5 billion kilometers).", "5.", "The average distance from the Earth to the Sun is about 93 m